          %h1#the_lambert__function
            The Lambert
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_1.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            function
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#lambert__and_rooted_trees"}
                  Lambert
                  %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_2.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                  and rooted trees
              %li
                %a{:href => "#counting_rooted_trees"} Counting rooted trees
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+analysis"} complex analysis
            = succeed "-function" do
              %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_3.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multivalued+function"} multi-branched function
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+function"} inverse
            to the function
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_4.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi z
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(z) = z e^z
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree"} rooted trees
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrange+inversion+formula"} Lagrange inversion formula
          %p
            We have
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_5.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(z) e^{W(z)} = z
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_6.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z = 0
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_7.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(z)
            as a formal
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+series"} power series
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_8.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mn ∞
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi n
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %msup
                        %mi z
                        %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo !
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(z) = \sum_{n = 1}^{\infty} \frac{(-n)^{n-1} z^n}{n!} .
          %p A proof of this formula is sketched below.
          %h2#lambert__and_rooted_trees
            Lambert
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_9.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            and rooted trees
          %p
            Let
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_10.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(X)
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/species"} species
            of rooted trees. Choosing a structure of rooted tree
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_11.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            (on a finite set of vertices) amounts to
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Choosing one vertex to serve as the root of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_12.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %li
              %p Choosing a structure of “rooted forest” (a disjoint collection of rooted trees) on the complement of the root.
          %p The idea is that given a rooted forest, we get a rooted tree by adding in a new vertex (which serves as root) and drawing an edge from each root of the forest to the new vertex.
          %p This observation leads to the structural isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_13.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(X) = X \otimes \exp(R(X))
          %p
            Let
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_14.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi n
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(x) = \sum_{n \geq 0} \frac{a_n x^n}{n!}
            be the formal power series corresponding to the generating function of
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_15.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(X)
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_16.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_n
            counts the number of rooted trees on
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_17.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            vertices. We may call
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_18.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(x)
            the
            %em cardinality
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_19.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(X)
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_20.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi x
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(x) = x e^{R(x)}
          %p or
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_21.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(x) e^{-R(x)} = x
          %p
            which means, after a short series of algebraic manipulations, that
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_22.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(x)
            is related to the Lambert
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_23.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            function as follows:
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_24.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(x) = - W(-x).
          %h2#counting_rooted_trees Counting rooted trees
          %p
            The number of possible rooted tree structures on
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_25.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            labeled vertices is
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_26.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n^{n-1}
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_27.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi W
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo ≥
                              %mn 1
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi n
                                %mrow
                                  %mi n
                                  %mo −
                                  %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mi x
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mi n
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo !
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo ≥
                              %mn 1
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mi n
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mrow
                                  %mi n
                                  %mo −
                                  %mn 1
                              %msup
                                %mi x
                                %mi n
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  W(x) &amp; = &amp; - R(-x) \\
                  \&amp; = &amp; - \sum_{n \geq 1} \frac{n^{n-1} (-x)^n}{n!} \\
                  \&amp; = &amp; \sum_{n \geq 1} \frac{(-n)^{n-1} x^n}{n!}
                  }
          %p as claimed earlier.
          %p
            In fact, Joyal counts the number of
            %em bipointed
            trees (trees equipped with an ordered pair of vertices, possibly the same one), and shows this is the same as the number of endofunctions on an
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_28.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            element set. Since this is
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_29.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi n
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n^n
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_30.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi n
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n^2
            = succeed "-element" do
              %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_31.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_32.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n^{n-2}
            = succeed "." do
              %strong Cayley’s theorem
            %em rooted
            trees is
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_33.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msup
                      %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \cdot n^{n-2} = n^{n-1}
          %p
            For a bipointed tree
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_34.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_35.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo ,
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (t, h)
            where
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_36.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            is called a
            %em tail
            and
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_37.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            a
            = succeed "." do
              %em head
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_38.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            to
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_39.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            is endowed with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+order"} linear order
            (namely, the order in which they appear on the path, with
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_40.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            first). We call this ordered set the
            %em spine
            of the bipointed tree. At the same time, each vertex
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_41.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            along the spine is the root of a rooted tree
            = succeed ":" do
              %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_42.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_v
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_43.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
            of
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_44.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            belongs to
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_45.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_v
            if the unique path from
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_46.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
            to
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_47.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            first meets the spine at
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_48.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
          %p
            A choice of bipointed tree structure on a finite set
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_49.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            can thus be equivalently described as follows:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Partition
                %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_50.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                into one or more subsets (which are equivalence classes);
            %li
              %p
                Choose a rooted tree structure on each class (if the root is
                = succeed "," do
                  %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_51.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
                = succeed ");" do
                  %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_52.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi T
                          %mi v
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_v
            %li
              %p Choose a way of linearly ordering the equivalence classes (which is really the same as linearly ordering the roots).
          %p
            If
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_53.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is the species of linearly ordered sets, and
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_54.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is the species of rooted trees, this way of describing bipointed trees establishes an explicit bijection between
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_55.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \circ R
            and the species of bipointed trees.
          %p
            For an endofunction
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_56.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon S \to S
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_57.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            be the intersection of images of iterates
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_58.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{(n)}(S)
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_59.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi K
                  %mo →
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon K \to K
            is a surjection and therefore a bijection (permutation). Picturing an endofunction as a graph (where an edge is drawn between
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_60.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            and
            = succeed ")," do
              %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_61.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(s)
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_62.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in K
            is the root of a rooted tree
            = succeed ":" do
              %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_63.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_v
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_64.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
            belongs to
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_65.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_v
            if
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_66.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{(n)}(w) = v
            for some
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_67.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_68.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{(k)}(w)
            does not belong to
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_69.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_70.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \lt n
          %p
            A choice of endofunction structure on
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_71.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            can thus be equivalently described as follows:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Partition
                %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_72.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                into one or more subsets (equivalence classes);
            %li
              %p
                Choose a rooted tree structure on each class (if the root is
                = succeed "," do
                  %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_73.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
                = succeed ");" do
                  %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_74.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi T
                          %mi v
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_v
            %li
              %p
                Choose a permutation on the set of equivalence classes (tantamount to a permutation of the roots
                = succeed ")." do
                  %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_75.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
          %p
            If
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_76.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is the species of permutations, and
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_77.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            the species of rooted trees, this establishes an explicit bijection between
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_78.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \circ R
            and the species of endofunctions.
          %p
            Since the species
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_79.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            of linear orderings and the species
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_80.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            of permutations have the same cardinality, it follows that the species
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_81.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \circ R
            and
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_82.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \circ R
            also have the same cardinality, which is to say that the number of bipointed tree structures on
            %math#mathml_40a663f2f5a8de69145e89a151d888e3a09e0c0b_83.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            equals the number of endofunctions, as was to be proved.
